From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32: let SwitchToThisWindow bring an external shell's task to the foreground

Purpose: switch tasks from the ReactOS shell's taskbar in the Wayland
session.
Windows behavior: SwitchToThisWindow restores a minimized window or brings
it to the top, and makes it the foreground window. ReactOS's taskbar
(base/shell/explorer/taskswnd.cpp) switches tasks with it alone.
Wine before: it only restored or raised the window. In the X11 session
bridge-wm activates every window it maps, but win4wine's labwc leaves a
window that Wine maps with _NET_WM_USER_TIME 0 inactive, so a restored
window stayed inactive and the taskbar's next click restored it again
instead of minimizing it.
Change: with the opt-in, also call SetForegroundWindow.
Evidence: minimize and restore four times from ReactOS's taskbar in the
nested Wayland session and in the X11 session.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
---
 dlls/user32/win.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/user32/win.c b/dlls/user32/win.c
index 98fd0f8..dd7618c 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/win.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/win.c
@@ -696,6 +696,9 @@ void WINAPI SwitchToThisWindow( HWND hwnd, BOOL alt_tab )
 {
     if (IsIconic( hwnd )) NtUserShowWindow( hwnd, SW_RESTORE );
     else BringWindowToTop( hwnd );
+    /* Windows also makes it the foreground window; an external shell's
+     * taskbar (ReactOS's) switches tasks with this alone. */
+    if (win4wine_external_shell()) NtUserSetForegroundWindow( hwnd );
 }
 
 
